  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CEPEW-VATJ Tax policy reform</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This actor will contribute to improve the living standards of marginalized groups and promote gender equality via better tax policies in the extractive industry in Vietnam. During this process, the project also build capacity for the members of VATJ, so that theycan monitor policies and practices, as well as engage effectively into policy dialogues with enterprises and authorities.

Besides,VATJ will also contribute to apply international standards into Vietnam to protect the rights of women and other marginalized groups working in extractive industry.

VATJ will collaborate with other CSOs to build new indicators to rank the transparency and accountability of 63 provinces, produce researches and policy briefs, shadow reports, and run communicationcampaigns to push demand on authorities. By using evidence-based findings and mobilizing the public, this project aims to reform tax and fees on natural resources,raise awareness of the public on tax and budget policies, as well as promote transparency and accountability of local authorities.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="90">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Center for Education Promotion and Empowerment of Women (CEPEW) is a Vietnamese Non-governmental organization established in 1997. Promotion and protection women human rights in particular and human right , universal values in general  and enabling civilsociety environment are two of CEPEW#s priorities. So that, CEPEW is an active member of People#s Participation Working Group, Cooperation Group for Governance and Administration Reform (GPAR) and Gender and Community Development Network (GENCOMNET). In recent years, CEPEWhas coordinated hundreds civil society organizations to develop join submission on human rights implementation in Vietnam under Universal Periodic Review Mechanism of UN Human Rights Council and stakeholders# report on implementation ofConvention on Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination against Women (CEDAW) and presented it to CEDAW Committee in Geneva. CEPEW has also applied international human rights standards and universal values for policy advocacy in Vietnam.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Center for Education Promotion and</narrative>
